    "content": "Caasha Geelle Diiriye, who previously served as Puntland's Minister of Women's Affairs and held various positions in Somalia, has spoken out about the effects of recent heavy rains in Galkacyo. She emphasized the need for immediate action to mitigate the impact on residents. The rains have caused significant flooding in the city, affecting daily life and infrastructure.\n\nGalkacyo, a major city in the Mudug region, is divided between Puntland and Galmudug. The city has a history of flooding due to poor drainage systems and rapid urbanization. In recent years, seasonal rains have repeatedly caused displacement and property damage, prompting calls for better urban planning and disaster response.\n\nGeelle, known for her advocacy on women's and social issues, has been vocal about the need for government accountability and community resilience. Her statement comes amid growing concerns about the lack of adequate infrastructure to cope with recurrent floods. Local authorities have yet to announce comprehensive measures to address the situation.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the flooding in Galkacyo is a reminder of the challenges faced by relatives back home. Many diaspora members send remittances to support families affected by natural disasters. The recurring floods also hinder economic activities, exacerbating hardships for a population already vulnerable to conflict and climate shocks.\n\nAs the rains continue, residents and officials must work together to find sustainable solutions. Improved drainage, early warning systems, and coordinated response efforts are essential to protect lives and livelihoods. The diaspora can play a role by supporting local initiatives and advocating for long-term resilience.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/caasha-geelle-oo-si-adag-uga-hadashay-saamaynta-biyaha-roobka-ee-magaalada-galkacyo/426485/",
